            "review_title": "Review at Mirai",
            "review_text": "PetitRed\nHo Chi Minh City, null, Vietnam2 contributions\n0\nI love bamboo charcoal dishes\nNov 2014 • Friends\nRecent discovery of the first Japanese restaurant using bamboo charcoal as healthy homemade noodle concept here in the central of Sai Gon. \n\n\"Black and Sparkling\", my friend's surprised expression while seeing the black udon for the very first time of our life. The taste will be something you have never experienced before. Calcium-filled tasty noodle will be on your dining table. I am not the fans of fried food but the combination between this kind of udon and tempura is so lovely. You will experience crispier flavor by submerging the bamboo charcoal. The savor of fried food will be so fresh with true aroma of the ingredients\n\nI have been to Japan and it's not easy to find the homemade charcoal noodle. So surprised to see this restaurant in Viet Nam. \n\nHighly recommendation\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 18, 2014",
